warning[E0214]: append on parameter 'buf' may alias the caller's backing array
 --> lint_append_param_alias.bit:7:3
  |
7 |   append(buf, 1)
  |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ if 'buf' is owned by this function, silence just this call with `// bit:lint allow E0214 -- <reason>` on the line above, or the whole file with `// bit:lint disable append-aliasing -- <reason>` in the leading comment block; otherwise make the growth reach the caller by returning it: `return buf` (or a struct/bundle field carrying it) — `buf = append(buf, ...)` alone does NOT propagate out of this function
